## Algorithms
A. Stack Algorithm
Start and initialize top = -1.
Push: Check if the stack is full. If not, insert the member at the top.
Pop: Check if the stack is empty. If not, remove the top member.
Display: Print all members from top to bottom.
Repeat until the user exits.
B. Queue Algorithm
Start and initialize front = 0 and rear = -1.
Enqueue: Check if the queue is full. If not, insert the member at the rear.
Dequeue: Check if the queue is empty. If not, remove the front member.
Display: Print all members from front to rear.
Repeat until the user exits.
C. Main Algorithm
Start the program.
Display the main menu: Stack, Queue, and Exit.
If Stack is selected, display its operations and perform the chosen operation.
If Queue is selected, display its operations and perform the chosen operation.
Repeat the menu until Exit is selected.
Stop the program.
